## Why this is a Given and not the product's work

The body performs no arithmetic and runs no calculator command: it only records
*which* Go tool the later `when` step will invoke and the environment that tool
needs. The halving itself stays in `halving.go`, which runs
`<toolchain> run ./services/calc halve VALUE` from the host root, exactly as the
`halve` command is declared in `docs/architecture/calc-cli.yaml`. The observable
effect the Word mapping names — "The halving step runs the calculator's halve
command with it" — comes from `State.Go`, which that step already reads.

## Note on the environment

`ToolchainEnv` starts from `os.Environ()` on purpose, so `PATH`, `HOME`,
`GOCACHE`, `GOMODCACHE` and `GOFLAGS` are inherited rather than replaced; the
stand-in turns module downloads off with `GOPROXY=off`, so it depends on that
inherited module cache. `CALC_REAL_GO` is appended last, so it wins over any
inherited value of the same name.

